import FX1Poly.Polygraph.TwoCategory.Brauer.WiringDescReachable

/-! # KEYSTONE6 brick (B) — `BrauerConv`, the diagram-sound convertibility relation over the presentation

The Brauer presentation ships as data (`brauerPresentation`, `Brauer/WiringDesc.lean`) with per-relation
diagram-soundness witnesses.  This file turns those witnesses into an inductive CONVERTIBILITY relation
`BrauerConv` on generator words and proves it DIAGRAM-SOUND: convertible words induce the same `DiagramType`
(boundary perfect-matching + loop count).

## What `BrauerConv` contains (each constructor genuinely diagram-sound, zero-axiom)

  * **The equivalence closure** — `refl` / `symm` / `trans` (soundness by `Eq.refl` / `Eq.symm` / `Eq.trans`).
  * **The five Brauer relations at their boundary** — `snake` / `snakeMirror` / `crossingInvolution` /
    `yangBaxter` / `capSlide` (soundness by the shipped `*_diagram_sound` witnesses).
  * ★ **The interchange (Godement) move, IN ARBITRARY CONTEXT** — `interchange`: two generators fired at an
    in-range disjoint pair AFTER any prefix word commute.  This is the keystone move, and — unlike the five
    relations — it is discharged STATE-PARAMETRICALLY at every reachable prefix state by the brick-(A) reachable
    interchange `brauer_reachable_interchange` (which threads `fresh` / `forest` / `nfPos` / `bottomLe` through the
    whole `processBrauer` fold).  So the Godement law is a fully-contextual convertibility move here.

## Soundness + non-vacuity

  * ★ **`brauerConv_sound`** — `BrauerConv n a b → brauerDiagramOf n a = brauerDiagramOf n b`, by induction on the
    convertibility derivation; the interchange case reduces through `processBrauer_append` (foldl over `++`) to the
    brick-(A) reachable interchange.
  * NON-VACUOUS: `BrauerConv` genuinely relates DISTINCT words (`brauerConv_yangBaxter`, the two Yang–Baxter words),
    the discriminator genuinely SEPARATES (`brauerDiagram_crossing_ne_identity`: the crossing diagram `[3,2,1,0]` ≠
    the identity-pair diagram `[2,3,0,1]`), and `BrauerConv` is a PROPER relation
    (`brauerConv_crossing_not_identity`: the crossing is NOT convertible to the identity pair — else soundness would
    equate their distinct diagrams).

## The contextual WHISKER (congruence) move + the collapsed residual (`fxBrauer_hasBrauerSoundness` STAYS `false`)

  * ★ **The whisker (congruence) move** — `whisker`: two words fired after ANY prefix are convertible when, at the two
    post-prefix states, they preserve the BOUNDARY connectivity view (equal open-wire count, equal loop count, same
    boundary same-component relation on the in-range indices).  It gates on the STRUCTURAL union-find view
    (`matchingSameComponent`), NOT on the diagram conclusion, so it is non-circular; discharged uniformly in
    `brauerConv_sound` by `processBrauer_append` + `extractDiagram_eq_of_connectivityView`.  NON-VACUOUS:
    `brauerConv_whisker_crossingInvolution_inContext` fires R2 whiskered at offset `1` after a prefix crossing.

FULL Brauer soundness — the whole free-symmetric-self-dual congruence closure, i.e. whiskering the FIVE relations in
ARBITRARY horizontal context — rides ONE uniform residual now, not five: for each relation, its per-relation BOUNDARY
same-component preservation (`relationAgrees` — the union-find window-locality: firing the relation word in an
in-range window preserves the boundary partition, +length +loops), the EXACT hypothesis the `whisker` constructor
consumes.  Each relation is proven diagram-sound only at its OWN boundary/seed (`rfl` / staged witnesses), and the
uniform `relationAgrees` over every reachable state / offset is the crossing-inclusive analog of the arc route's
boundary-discipline / trace-equivalence subsystem (`fxMode_hasBoundaryDisciplinedSoundness`) — not yet built.
Concrete states discharge `relationAgrees` by `decide`; the uniform proof is the standing brick.  So `BrauerConv` is
the genuine convertibility generated by { equivalence, the five relations at the boundary, contextual interchange,
ANY connectivity-preserving contextual whisker }, PROVEN sound; flipping `fxBrauer_hasBrauerSoundness` needs the five
relations' uniform `relationAgrees` fed to the shipped `whisker` move.  `= false`, sharpened + residual collapsed
5→1.

Raw Lean 4 + Init; structural recursion, no `omega` / `simp`-AC / `native_decide` / `WellFounded.fix`.
Per-declaration `#assert_no_axioms` in the audit twin. -/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace FX1Poly.Polygraph

/-! ## `processBrauer` is a fold — it splits over word concatenation -/

/-- ★ **`processBrauer` splits over word concatenation** — the diagram fold of `atoms1 ++ atoms2` from a state is
the fold of `atoms2` from the fold of `atoms1` (`List.foldl` over `++`).  Structural on the first word. -/
theorem processBrauer_append :
    (atoms1 : List BrauerAtom) → (state : WireState) → (atoms2 : List BrauerAtom) →
    processBrauer state (atoms1 ++ atoms2) = processBrauer (processBrauer state atoms1) atoms2
  | [], _, _ => rfl
  | atom :: rest, state, atoms2 => processBrauer_append rest (stepBrauerAtom state atom) atoms2

/-! ## The convertibility relation -/

/-- ★ **`BrauerConv n a b`** — the diagram-sound convertibility of two generator words over `n` bottom wires: the
equivalence closure of the five Brauer relations (at their boundary) together with the fully-contextual interchange
(Godement) move. -/
inductive BrauerConv : Nat → List BrauerAtom → List BrauerAtom → Prop
  /-- Reflexivity. -/
  | refl (bottomCount : Nat) (word : List BrauerAtom) : BrauerConv bottomCount word word
  /-- Symmetry. -/
  | symm {bottomCount : Nat} {leftWord rightWord : List BrauerAtom} :
      BrauerConv bottomCount leftWord rightWord → BrauerConv bottomCount rightWord leftWord
  /-- Transitivity. -/
  | trans {bottomCount : Nat} {leftWord midWord rightWord : List BrauerAtom} :
      BrauerConv bottomCount leftWord midWord → BrauerConv bottomCount midWord rightWord →
      BrauerConv bottomCount leftWord rightWord
  /-- S1 snake straightening. -/
  | snake : BrauerConv snakeRelation.boundaryCount snakeRelation.lhs snakeRelation.rhs
  /-- S2 mirror snake straightening. -/
  | snakeMirror : BrauerConv snakeMirrorRelation.boundaryCount snakeMirrorRelation.lhs snakeMirrorRelation.rhs
  /-- R2 crossing involutivity. -/
  | crossingInvolution :
      BrauerConv crossingInvolutionRelation.boundaryCount crossingInvolutionRelation.lhs
        crossingInvolutionRelation.rhs
  /-- R3 Yang–Baxter. -/
  | yangBaxter : BrauerConv yangBaxterRelation.boundaryCount yangBaxterRelation.lhs yangBaxterRelation.rhs
  /-- R1 cap slides past a crossing. -/
  | capSlide : BrauerConv capSlideRelation.boundaryCount capSlideRelation.lhs capSlideRelation.rhs
  /-- ★ The interchange (Godement) move, IN ARBITRARY CONTEXT: after any prefix word, two generators fired at an
  in-range disjoint pair commute. -/
  | interchange (bottomCount : Nat) (prefixAtoms : List BrauerAtom) (positionA positionB : Nat)
      (descA descB : WiringDesc) :
      0 < bottomCount →
      positionA + descA.inputCount ≤ positionB →
      positionB + descB.inputCount
          ≤ (processBrauer (brauerSeed bottomCount) prefixAtoms).openWires.length →
      BrauerConv bottomCount
        (prefixAtoms ++ [⟨positionA, descA⟩,
          ⟨positionB - descA.inputCount + descA.outputCount, descB⟩])
        (prefixAtoms ++ [⟨positionB, descB⟩, ⟨positionA, descA⟩])
  /-- ★ The **contextual whisker (congruence) move**: two generator words fired after ANY prefix are convertible when,
  at the two post-prefix states, they preserve the BOUNDARY connectivity view — equal open-wire count, equal loop
  count, and the SAME boundary same-component relation on the in-range indices.  This is the uniform closure move: it
  gates on the STRUCTURAL union-find boundary view (`matchingSameComponent`), NOT on the diagram conclusion, so it is
  non-circular; discharged in `brauerConv_sound` by `processBrauer_append` + `extractDiagram_eq_of_connectivityView`.
  Every one of the five relations, whiskered in arbitrary context, is an instance ONCE its per-relation boundary
  same-component preservation (`relationAgrees`) is proven — the standing residual, now collapsed from five separate
  proofs to ONE uniform obligation over this move. -/
  | whisker (bottomCount : Nat) (prefixAtoms wordLeft wordRight : List BrauerAtom) :
      (processBrauer (processBrauer (brauerSeed bottomCount) prefixAtoms) wordLeft).openWires.length
          = (processBrauer (processBrauer (brauerSeed bottomCount) prefixAtoms) wordRight).openWires.length →
      (processBrauer (processBrauer (brauerSeed bottomCount) prefixAtoms) wordLeft).loops
          = (processBrauer (processBrauer (brauerSeed bottomCount) prefixAtoms) wordRight).loops →
      (∀ firstIndex secondIndex,
          firstIndex < bottomCount
              + (processBrauer (processBrauer (brauerSeed bottomCount) prefixAtoms) wordLeft).openWires.length →
          secondIndex < bottomCount
              + (processBrauer (processBrauer (brauerSeed bottomCount) prefixAtoms) wordLeft).openWires.length →
          matchingSameComponent bottomCount
              (processBrauer (processBrauer (brauerSeed bottomCount) prefixAtoms) wordLeft) firstIndex secondIndex
            = matchingSameComponent bottomCount
              (processBrauer (processBrauer (brauerSeed bottomCount) prefixAtoms) wordRight)
                firstIndex secondIndex) →
      BrauerConv bottomCount (prefixAtoms ++ wordLeft) (prefixAtoms ++ wordRight)

/-! ## Soundness -/

/-- ★ **`BrauerConv` is diagram-sound.**  Convertible words induce the SAME `DiagramType`.  By induction on the
derivation: the equivalence closure by `Eq`, the five relations by their shipped `*_diagram_sound` witnesses, and
the interchange move by reducing through `processBrauer_append` to the brick-(A) reachable interchange
`brauer_reachable_interchange`. -/
theorem brauerConv_sound {bottomCount : Nat} {leftWord rightWord : List BrauerAtom}
    (conv : BrauerConv bottomCount leftWord rightWord) :
    brauerDiagramOf bottomCount leftWord = brauerDiagramOf bottomCount rightWord := by
  induction conv with
  | refl _ _ => rfl
  | symm _ ih => exact ih.symm
  | trans _ _ ihLeft ihRight => exact ihLeft.trans ihRight
  | snake => exact snake_diagram_sound
  | snakeMirror => exact snakeMirror_diagram_sound
  | crossingInvolution => exact crossingInvolution_diagram_sound
  | yangBaxter => exact yangBaxter_diagram_sound
  | capSlide => exact capSlide_diagram_sound
  | interchange bottomCount prefixAtoms positionA positionB descA descB bottomPos disjoint windowB =>
      show extractDiagram bottomCount
          (processBrauer (brauerSeed bottomCount)
            (prefixAtoms ++ [⟨positionA, descA⟩,
              ⟨positionB - descA.inputCount + descA.outputCount, descB⟩]))
        = extractDiagram bottomCount
          (processBrauer (brauerSeed bottomCount)
            (prefixAtoms ++ [⟨positionB, descB⟩, ⟨positionA, descA⟩]))
      rw [processBrauer_append prefixAtoms (brauerSeed bottomCount)
            [⟨positionA, descA⟩, ⟨positionB - descA.inputCount + descA.outputCount, descB⟩],
        processBrauer_append prefixAtoms (brauerSeed bottomCount)
            [⟨positionB, descB⟩, ⟨positionA, descA⟩]]
      exact brauer_reachable_interchange bottomCount bottomPos prefixAtoms positionA positionB descA descB
        disjoint windowB
  | whisker bottomCount prefixAtoms wordLeft wordRight lengthsAgree loopsAgree relationAgrees =>
      show extractDiagram bottomCount
          (processBrauer (brauerSeed bottomCount) (prefixAtoms ++ wordLeft))
        = extractDiagram bottomCount
          (processBrauer (brauerSeed bottomCount) (prefixAtoms ++ wordRight))
      rw [processBrauer_append prefixAtoms (brauerSeed bottomCount) wordLeft,
        processBrauer_append prefixAtoms (brauerSeed bottomCount) wordRight]
      exact extractDiagram_eq_of_connectivityView bottomCount
        (processBrauer (processBrauer (brauerSeed bottomCount) prefixAtoms) wordLeft)
        (processBrauer (processBrauer (brauerSeed bottomCount) prefixAtoms) wordRight)
        lengthsAgree loopsAgree relationAgrees

/-! ## Non-vacuity -/

/-- `BrauerConv` genuinely relates DISTINCT words: the two Yang–Baxter words `(X⊗id)(id⊗X)(X⊗id)` and
`(id⊗X)(X⊗id)(id⊗X)` (which are different lists) are convertible. -/
theorem brauerConv_yangBaxter : BrauerConv 3 yangBaxterLhsWord yangBaxterRhsWord := BrauerConv.yangBaxter

/-- The diagram discriminator genuinely SEPARATES: the crossing diagram `[3,2,1,0]` differs from the identity-pair
diagram `[2,3,0,1]`.  So `brauerDiagramOf` is a non-constant, discriminating invariant. -/
theorem brauerDiagram_crossing_ne_identity :
    brauerDiagramOf 2 [crossingAt 0] ≠ brauerDiagramOf 2 [identityStrandAt 0, identityStrandAt 1] := by
  rw [crossing_diagram, identity_pair_diagram]; decide

/-- ★ **`BrauerConv` is a PROPER relation** — the crossing is NOT convertible to the identity pair.  If it were,
`brauerConv_sound` would equate their genuinely-distinct diagrams (`brauerDiagram_crossing_ne_identity`).  So
soundness is non-vacuous: it genuinely constrains which words are convertible. -/
theorem brauerConv_crossing_not_identity :
    ¬ BrauerConv 2 [crossingAt 0] [identityStrandAt 0, identityStrandAt 1] :=
  fun conv => brauerDiagram_crossing_ne_identity (brauerConv_sound conv)

/-! ## Non-vacuity of the whisker move — a relation whiskered IN CONTEXT

The whisker constructor is genuinely inhabited beyond the seed relations: here R2 (crossing involutivity) fired at
OFFSET 1 (on strands 1,2 of a three-strand boundary) — a left-identity whiskering the seed R2 (fixed at offset 0,
boundary 2) does NOT provide — AFTER a non-trivial prefix crossing, discharged by `decide` on the concrete
post-prefix states.  So `BrauerConv` genuinely contains contextual whiskerings of the relations. -/

/-- The boundary same-component agreement for R2-at-offset-1 after a prefix crossing, in the
`Nat.decidableBallLT`-friendly order (guard immediately after each binder), discharged by `decide`. -/
private theorem whiskerCrossingInvolution_relationAgrees_ordered : ∀ firstIndex,
    firstIndex < 3
        + (processBrauer (processBrauer (brauerSeed 3) [crossingAt 0]) [crossingAt 1, crossingAt 1]).openWires.length →
    ∀ secondIndex,
    secondIndex < 3
        + (processBrauer (processBrauer (brauerSeed 3) [crossingAt 0]) [crossingAt 1, crossingAt 1]).openWires.length →
    matchingSameComponent 3
        (processBrauer (processBrauer (brauerSeed 3) [crossingAt 0]) [crossingAt 1, crossingAt 1])
        firstIndex secondIndex
      = matchingSameComponent 3
        (processBrauer (processBrauer (brauerSeed 3) [crossingAt 0]) ([] : List BrauerAtom))
        firstIndex secondIndex := by decide

/-- ★ **The whisker move is NON-VACUOUS: R2 whiskered in a non-trivial context.**  After a prefix crossing on
strands `0,1`, the crossing-involution relation fired at offset `1` (on strands `1,2`) is convertible to the
identity — a genuinely contextual whiskering (offset `1`, three-strand boundary, non-empty prefix) that the five
seed constructors do not supply.  Its three connectivity obligations are discharged concretely by `decide` on the
post-prefix states. -/
theorem brauerConv_whisker_crossingInvolution_inContext :
    BrauerConv 3 ([crossingAt 0] ++ [crossingAt 1, crossingAt 1]) ([crossingAt 0] ++ ([] : List BrauerAtom)) :=
  BrauerConv.whisker 3 [crossingAt 0] [crossingAt 1, crossingAt 1] [] (by decide) (by decide)
    (fun firstIndex secondIndex hfirst hsecond =>
      whiskerCrossingInvolution_relationAgrees_ordered firstIndex hfirst secondIndex hsecond)

/-- The contextual whiskering above genuinely relates DISTINCT words (`[crossingAt 0, crossingAt 1, crossingAt 1]`
is not the singleton `[crossingAt 0]`), so the whisker move is a proper, inhabited closure operation. -/
theorem brauerConv_whisker_inContext_distinct :
    ([crossingAt 0] ++ [crossingAt 1, crossingAt 1]) ≠ ([crossingAt 0] ++ ([] : List BrauerAtom)) := by decide

/-! ## Honesty markers -/

/-- **Honesty marker — `BrauerConv` ships with a diagram-soundness proof.**  `brauerConv_sound` proves convertible
words induce the same `DiagramType`; the relation is the equivalence closure of the five Brauer relations (at their
boundary) plus the fully-contextual interchange (Godement) move, the latter discharged state-parametrically by the
brick-(A) `brauer_reachable_interchange`.  NON-VACUOUS: it relates distinct words (`brauerConv_yangBaxter`), the
discriminator separates (`brauerDiagram_crossing_ne_identity`), and the relation is proper
(`brauerConv_crossing_not_identity`).  `= true`. -/
def fxBrauer_hasBrauerConvSoundness : Bool := true

/-- **Honesty marker — the interchange (Godement) move is FULLY CONTEXTUAL in `BrauerConv`.**  Unlike the five
relations (proven diagram-sound only at their own boundary/seed), the interchange constructor is discharged after
ANY prefix word via the brick-(A) reachable-state interchange (`brauer_reachable_interchange`, which threads
`fresh` / `forest` / `nfPos` / `bottomLe` through the whole fold).  So the crossing-inclusive Godement law is a
genuine contextual convertibility move.  `= true`. -/
def fxBrauer_hasBrauerConvContextualInterchange : Bool := true

/-- ★ **Honesty marker — the contextual WHISKER (congruence) move is SHIPPED and NON-VACUOUS.**  The `whisker`
constructor closes `BrauerConv` under: two words fired after ANY prefix are convertible when, at the two post-prefix
states, they preserve the BOUNDARY connectivity view (equal open-wire count, equal loops, same boundary
same-component relation on the in-range indices).  It gates on the STRUCTURAL union-find view (`matchingSameComponent`),
NOT on the diagram conclusion, so it is NON-CIRCULAR, and it is discharged in `brauerConv_sound` uniformly by
`processBrauer_append` + `extractDiagram_eq_of_connectivityView`.  NON-VACUOUS: `brauerConv_whisker_crossingInvolution_inContext`
exhibits R2 whiskered at offset `1` after a prefix crossing (`brauerConv_whisker_inContext_distinct` confirms the two
words are distinct).  This is the uniform closure move: EVERY one of the five relations whiskered in arbitrary
context is an instance ONCE its per-relation boundary same-component preservation is proven.  `= true`. -/
def fxBrauer_hasBrauerWhiskerMove : Bool := true

/-- **Honesty marker — FULL Brauer soundness (the whole congruence closure) STAYS `false`, residual COLLAPSED to ONE
uniform obligation.**  `brauerConv_sound` now covers { equivalence, the five relations AT THE BOUNDARY, contextual
interchange, ANY connectivity-preserving contextual whisker }.  The FULL free-symmetric-self-dual congruence closure
additionally whiskers the FIVE relations in ARBITRARY horizontal context.  With the `whisker` move shipped, that is
no longer five separate state-parametric bricks: it is ONE uniform residual — for each relation, its per-relation
BOUNDARY same-component preservation `relationAgrees` (the union-find window-locality: firing the relation word in an
in-range window preserves the boundary partition, +length +loops), the exact hypothesis the `whisker` constructor
consumes.  The interchange discharges it via `blockRotate`; the five relations discharge it via the un-built
per-relation window-locality (crossing-inclusive analog of the arc route's boundary-discipline subsystem
`fxMode_hasBoundaryDisciplinedSoundness`).  Concrete states discharge it by `decide`
(`brauerConv_whisker_crossingInvolution_inContext`); the uniform (all reachable states / offsets) proof is the
residual.  So `fxBrauer_hasBrauerSoundness` STAYS `false`, its residual now precisely = the five relations' uniform
`relationAgrees` over the shipped `whisker` move.  `= true`. -/
def fxBrauer_hasBrauerSoundnessResidualNamed : Bool := true

end FX1Poly.Polygraph
